"{\n  \"agreementDate\": \"___ day of ________ Two Thousand Two\",\n  \"placeOfSigning\": \"\",\n  \"supporting_documents\": [],\n  \"parties\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Council of Scientific and Industrial Research (CSIR) / Central Salt and Marine Chemicals Research Institute (CSMCRI)\",\n      \"address\": \"Anusandhan Bhavan, 2, Rafi Marg, New Delhi-110 001; Central Salt & Marine Chemicals Research Institute, G. B. Marg, Bhavnagar – 364002, Gujarat\",\n      \"phone\": \"\",\n      \"email\": \"\",\n      \"CIN\": \"\",\n      \"PAN\": \"\",\n      \"GST\": \"\",\n      \"obligations\": [\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.4.1\",\n          \"description\": \"Undertake the work on the PROJECT as per the objectives detailed in Annexure I.\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"CSMCRI shall undertake the work on the PROJECT as per the objectives detailed in Annexure I.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.4.2\",\n          \"description\": \"Complete the work as per schedule of work as detailed in Annexure I. Period of completion could be extended by mutual agreement without additional payment.\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"CSMCRI shall complete the work as per schedule of work as detailed in Annexure I. This period of completion of work could however be extended to such further periods as may be mutually agreed to between the parties without any additional payment by the PARTY.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.4.3\",\n          \"description\": \"Submit progress reports at 6-monthly intervals and a detailed Final Report after conclusion of the project.\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"CSMCRI shall submit progress reports at 6-monthly intervals, starting from the commencement of Project and a detailed Final Report after conclusion of the project.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.4.4\",\n          \"description\": \"Not responsible for damage to PARTY's property by PARTY's personnel; responsible for damage caused by its own personnel.\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"CSMCRI shall not be responsible for any damage to the property/plant/material of the PARTY by PARTY'S personnel during or consequent to the work if any carried out under the PROJECT in PARTY'S premises. However CSMCRI shall be responsible for any damage caused due to any action or inaction of its personnel including loss of property, life, etc.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.7.5\",\n          \"description\": \"Consult PARTY and obtain written consent for any publication in respect of the PROJECT.\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"CSMCRI shall consult the PARTY and obtain written consent for any publication in respect of the PROJECT. CSMCRI shall acknowledge the PARTY in all such publications.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Strides Arcolabs Limited\",\n      \"address\": \"Strides House, Bilekahalli, Bannerghatta Road, Bangalore - 560 076, INDIA\",\n      \"phone\": \"\",\n      \"email\": \"\",\n      \"CIN\": \"\",\n      \"PAN\": \"\",\n      \"GST\": \"\",\n      \"obligations\": [\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.5.1\",\n          \"description\": \"Mutually provide information to facilitate Project work and provide relevant information from time to time.\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"The PARTY and CSMCRI shall mutually provide information to each other on the work already carried out to facilitate the Project work (cf. ‘Work Elements’ in Annexure I). The PARTY shall also provide to CSMCRI any relevant information pertaining to the Project it may receive/collect from time to time.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.5.2\",\n          \"description\": \"Extend technical support wherever possible and required, upon request of CSMCRI.\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"The PARTY shall extend technical support wherever possible and required, upon the request of CSMCRI.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.5.3\",\n          \"description\": \"Return any equipment/instrument/hardware loaned by CSMCRI after completion of the PROJECT.\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"Any equipment/ instrument/ hardware etc. which may be loaned by the PARTY to CSMCRI or CSIR, or their employees or personnel, shall after the completion of the PROJECT be returned to the PARTY. Conversely, any equipment that may be loaned by CSMCRI to the PARTY for the purposes of the PROJECT shall be returned by the PARTY promptly.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.5.4\",\n          \"description\": \"Make all payments on time as per CL 2.1 and CL 2.2.\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"The PARTY shall make all payments on time as per CL 2.1 and CL 2.2.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"penalty_clauses\": [],\n  \"arbitration_clause\": {\n    \"amicable_settlement\": \"Any dispute or difference arising between the parties to this agreement in connection with this agreement or the implementation of the obligation arising therefrom shall be attempted to be resolved mutually.\",\n    \"arbitration\": \"If amicable settlement fails after reasonable attempts (not less than 60 days) and 30 days' notice, the dispute shall be referred to a sole Arbitrator or, in case of disagreement, to three Arbitrators (one appointed by each party, third by the two Arbitrators).\",\n    \"arbitral_tribunal\": \"Sole Arbitrator or three Arbitrators (one by each party, third by the two Arbitrators).\",\n    \"final_and_binding\": \"The Parties hereto shall submit to the Arbitrator's award and the award shall be enforceable in any competent court of law.\",\n    \"seat_and_venue\": \"Mumbai\",\n    \"language\": \"English\",\n    \"costs\": \"The Arbitrators shall also decide on the costs of the arbitration proceedings.\"\n  },\n  \"clauses\": [\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.1\",\n      \"description\": \"Scope of the Agreement\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"The agreement details the terms and conditions, financial arrangements, modalities of collaboration, intellectual property rights, responsibilities and obligations of the PARTY and CSMCRI pertaining to the PROJECT.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.2\",\n      \"description\": \"Financial Arrangements\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"The PARTY shall pay to CSMCRI a sum of Rs. 13,50,000/- (Rupees thirteen lakhs fifty thousand only) which shall be full and complete payment (irrespective of any overruns in time, if any) in consideration for the performance of the obligations of CSMCRI/CSIR, including the Work Elements (as specified in Annexure I) in accordance with the Activity Milestones (as specified in Annexure I) undertaken by CSMCRI as per the terms and conditions of this agreement, in four equal installments in the following manner: (i) 40% upon signing of the agreement (ii) 15% within fifteen days of submission of first report and invoice (iii) 15% within fifteen days of submission of second report and invoice (iv) 15% within fifteen days of submission of third report and invoice (v) 15% at the time of submission of final report and invoice. THE PARTY shall also reimburse reasonable travel costs of personnel from CSMCRI who may be deputed outside their place of work, i.e.at CSMCRI Bhavnagar, in connection with the PROJECT at the request of the PARTY. Such reimbursement shall be made at actuals, and upon the production of invoices showing travel costs incurred, wherever possible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.3\",\n      \"description\": \"Modalities of Project Execution\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"CSMCRI shall carry out the research activities as per the Work Elements and Activity Milestones in Annexure I and submit progress reports to the PARTY at regular intervals as specified in CL 4.3 below. The PARTY shall provide necessary support in those aspects of the Project where it has core strengths. CSMCRI and the PARTY shall jointly review progress and methodology and modify Project objectives as may be required during the course of the Project. The Project as set out in Annexure I shall be carried out and executed in two phases as per the time schedules as set out below: Phase I: CSMCRI shall at its site develop a gelatin substitute from carrageena with suitable rheological and tensile properties for making soft gelatin capsules. Phase II: Upon successful completion of Phase I, accelerated stability and stress tests shall be carried out at the Party’s premises to ensure the interchangeability of the gelatin substitute capsules so developed, with that of conventional gelatin capsules under the guidance of CSMCRI.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.4\",\n      \"description\": \"Responsibilities of CSMCRI\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"CSMCRI shall undertake the work on the PROJECT as per the objectives detailed in Annexure I. CSMCRI shall complete the work as per schedule of work as detailed in Annexure I. This period of completion of work could however be extended to such further periods as may be mutually agreed to between the parties without any additional payment by the PARTY. CSMCRI shall submit progress reports at 6-monthly intervals, starting from the commencement of Project and a detailed Final Report after conclusion of the project. CSMCRI shall not be responsible for any damage to the property/plant/material of the PARTY by PARTY'S personnel during or consequent to the work if any carried out under the PROJECT in PARTY'S premises. However CSMCRI shall be responsible for any damage caused due to any action or inaction of its personnel including loss of property, life, etc.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.5\",\n      \"description\": \"Responsibilities of the PARTY\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"The PARTY and CSMCRI shall mutually provide information to each other on the work already carried out to facilitate the Project work (cf. ‘Work Elements’ in Annexure I). The PARTY shall also provide to CSMCRI any relevant information pertaining to the Project it may receive/collect from time to time. The PARTY shall extend technical support wherever possible and required, upon the request of CSMCRI. Any equipment/ instrument/ hardware etc. which may be loaned by the PARTY to CSMCRI or CSIR, or their employees or personnel, shall after the completion of the PROJECT be returned to the PARTY. Conversely, any equipment that may be loaned by CSMCRI to the PARTY for the purposes of the PROJECT shall be returned by the PARTY promptly. The PARTY shall make all payments on time as per CL 2.1 and CL 2.2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.6\",\n      \"description\": \"Completion\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"The PROJECT shall be deemed to have been successfully completed after completion of the following events: (a) submission of final report prepared by CSMCRI, after mutual consultation with PARTY. (b) after sufficient trial production of the seaweed based soft capsules is completed and the said capsules are subjected to accelerated studies and other stress tests to ensure that the product perform similarly to conventional gelatin when used in soft capsules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.7\",\n      \"description\": \"Results of Project\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"Any intellectual property rights, patents, design, trademark, copyrights obtained by the parties hereto pertaining to the PROJECT prior to signing of the agreement shall remain the exclusive property of that party alone. However, CSMCRI shall grant an irrevocable, royalty-free license to the PARTY to use its IPR, which may have been used to develop the deliverables under the Project for the purposes of use in relation to the Project. The intellectual property for the project work upto Phase I that is know how/ process/ design/patents/ copyrights generated in the PROJECT shall be the property of CSMCRI and licensed to the PARTY as part of know how transfer. Such license shall be granted exclusively to the PARTY during the period of limited exclusivity as per CL 9.1. CSMCRI and the PARTY agree that any intellectual property rights, patents, design, trademark, copyrights, know-how pertaining to the PROJECT developed during Phase II as detailed in CL. 3.2 above shall be the property of the PARTY alone. CSMCRI and the PARTY shall make applications for a global patent, and such application shall be filed jointly and the global patent, if and when obtained, shall be owned jointly by CSMCRI and the PARTY. The costs of such global patent filings shall be shared by the CSMCRI and the PARTY. CSMCRI shall consult the PARTY and obtain written consent for any publication in respect of the PROJECT. CSMCRI shall acknowledge the PARTY in all such publications.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.8\",\n      \"description\": \"Confidentiality\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"During the tenure of the agreement and three years thereafter both CSMCRI and PARTY undertake on their own behalf and on behalf of their subcontractors/employees/ representatives/ associates to maintain strict confidentiality and prevent disclosure thereof, of all the information and data exchanged/generated pertaining to work under this agreement for any purposes other than in accordance with this agreement. Both parties, however, retain rights to use the Research & Development results generated during the PROJECT for their own Research & Development programmes without any obligation to the other party, provided such use is non-commercial and not to the detriment of the other party. CSMSRI warrants, in particular, that the Research & Development results generated during the PROJECT is not disclosed, shared with or used in any similar Project for a competitor, rival or other pharmaceutical company.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.9\",\n      \"description\": \"Utilisation of Intellectual Property Developed\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"The PARTY shall have the first option to develop further/commercially exploit/use the intellectual property generated in the PROJECT for which a separate agreement shall be signed between CSMCRI and the PARTY provided such agreement is signed within twelve months from the date of completion of the PROJECT, or the date of receipt of regulatory approvals from agencies in India, USA, UK, Europe and Australia, whichever is earlier. The terms of this agreement, which shall include both know how transfer fee and annual royalty payments for seven years or lump sum royalty payment, shall be decided at the time of know how transfer and the amount of Rs 13.5 lakhs incurred towards the PROJECT by the PARTY shall be adjusted against the know how transfer fee. CSMCRI further agrees to grant a period of limited exclusivity not exceeding 5 (five) years from the date of completion of the PROJECT, or the date of receipt of regulatory approvals from agencies in India, USA, UK, Europe and Australia, whichever is earlier of commercially exploitable technology for a fee to be separately decided for this limited exclusivity. CSMCRI and the PARTY shall each have the right to license the know how generated in the PROJECT to a third party(ies) with the prior written concurrence of the other during the period of limited exclusivity beyond which CSMCRI shall have the sole right to transfer the know how to prospective clients. Provided that at no time CSMCRI shall grant a license of the know-how to an entity competing with the Party without the prior written consent of the Party. The premia/ royalty accrued from licensing of the intellectual property to other party(ies) during the period of limited exclusivity as per CL. 9.1 and CL. 9.2 shall be shared equally between CSMCRI and the PARTY. During the work envisaged under the agreement, in the event of CSMCRI exploring, inventing or discovering results other than the specific objectives of the PROJECT, CSMCRI shall retain absolute rights on such results. CSMCRI shall first offer such results to the PARTY on negotiated terms by entering into a separate agreement. In case the PARTY does not accept the offer, CSMCRI shall be free to release such results to other parties without any obligations to the PARTY.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.10\",\n      \"description\": \"Force Majeure\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"Neither party shall be held responsible for non-fulfillment of their respective obligations under this agreement due to the exigency of one or more of the force majeure events such as but not limited to Acts of God, war or threat of war, insurrection, rebellion, fire, floods/earthquakes or any other natural disaster or adverse weather conditions, strikes, lockout or any other labour unrest, epidemic, riots, civil commotion or political instability, act of terrorism, etc, provided on the occurrence and cessation of any such events, party affected thereby shall give notice in writing to the other party within one month of such occurrence or cessation. If the force majeure condition continues beyond six months, the parties shall then mutually decide about the future course of action.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.11\",\n      \"description\": \"Effective Date, Duration, Termination of Agreement\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"The agreement shall be effective from the Effective Date hereof. The agreement pertaining to execution of the PROJECT shall terminate as per the terms of CL. 4.2 whereas the agreement arrived at between the parties hereto for the utilization of the intellectual property shall remain in force as long as the terms specified in CL. 9 demand. During the tenure of the agreement, either party hereto may terminate the agreement (a) for breach of any of the terms and conditions of this agreement by the other party, or (b) unilaterally for unforeseen reasons arising out of force majeure circumstances by giving three month's notice in writing to the other party. In the event of the termination of the agreement vide CL 11.3, the rights and obligations of the parties shall be settled by mutual discussions; the financial settlement shall take into consideration not only the expenditure incurred at the date of termination, but also the expenditure committed by the parties hereto and the terms as outlined in CL 9.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.12\",\n      \"description\": \"Notices\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"All notices and other communications required to be served on the PARTY under the terms of this agreement shall be considered to be duly served if the same shall have been delivered to, left with or posted by registered mail to the PARTY at the address given below: Strides Arcolab Limited, Strides House, Bilekahalli, Bannerghatta Road, Bangalore-560 076 INDIA. Any notice to be given to the CSIR/CSMCRI shall be considered duly served if the same shall have been delivered to, left with, or posted by registered mail to the CSMCRI address given below: Central Salt & Marine Chemicals Research Institute, G. B. Marg, Bhavnagar – 364002, Gujarat.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.13\",\n      \"description\": \"Amendments to the Agreement\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"No amendment or modification of this agreement shall be valid unless the same is made in writing by the parties or their authorized representatives and specifically stating the same to be an amendment to this agreement. The modifications/changes shall be effective from the date on which they are made/executed, unless otherwise agreed to.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.14\",\n      \"description\": \"Assignment of the Agreement\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"The rights and/or liabilities arising to any party to this agreement shall not be assigned except with the written consent of the other parties and subject to such terms and conditions as may be mutually agreed upon.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.15\",\n      \"description\": \"Arbitration\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"Any dispute or difference arising between the parties to this agreement in connection with this agreement or the implementation of the obligation arising therefrom shall be attempted to be resolved mutually. The attempt to bring about an amicable settlement shall be treated as having failed as soon as one of the Parties hereto, after reasonable attempts, which shall continue for not less than sixty (60) days, gives thirty (30) days notice thereof to this effect to the other Party in writing. In case of such failure, the dispute shall be referred to a sole Arbitrator or in case of disagreement as to the appointment of the sole Arbitrator, to three (3) Arbitrators, of which each party shall appoint one (1) Arbitrator each, and the third Arbitrator shall be appointed by the two appointed Arbitrators. The Arbitration proceedings shall be held in Mumbai. The Arbitration proceedings shall be governed by the laws of India. The proceedings of Arbitration shall be in English language. The Arbitrator's award shall be substantiated in writing. The Arbitrators shall also decide on the costs of the arbitration proceedings. The Parties hereto shall submit to the Arbitrator's award and the award shall be enforceable in any competent court of law.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.16\",\n      \"description\": \"Governing Law\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"This agreement shall be interpreted and governed in all respects by the laws of India and the courts of Mumbai alone and no other courts shall be entitled to entertain and try any dispute or matter relating to or arising out of this agreement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.17\",\n      \"description\": \"Violation of Terms\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"The parties agree that either party shall be entitled to an injunction, restraining order, right for recovery, suit for specific performance or such other equitable relief as a court of competent jurisdiction may deem necessary or appropriate to restrain the other party from committing any violation or enforce the performance of the covenants, obligations and representations contained in this agreement. These injunctive remedies are cumulative and are in addition to any other rights and remedies the parties may have at law or in equity, including without limitation a right for recovery of the amounts due under this agreement and related costs and a right for damages.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.18\",\n      \"description\": \"Waiver\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"No failure or delay on the part of any of the parties to this agreement relating to the exercise of any right power privilege or remedy provided under this agreement shall operate as a waiver of such right power privilege or remedy or as a waiver of any preceding or succeeding breach by the other party to this agreement nor shall any single or partial exercise of any right power privilege or remedy preclude any other or further exercise of such or any other right power privilege or remedy provided in this agreement all of which are several and cumulative and are not exclusive of each other or of any other rights or remedies otherwise available to a party at law or in equity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.19\",\n      \"description\": \"No Partnership\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"None of the provisions of this agreement shall be deemed to constitute a partnership between the Parties hereto and none of the Parties shall have any authority to bind or shall be deemed to be the agent of the other in any way except as set out herein. The Parties to this agreement acknowledge that all transactions between the said Parties contemplated hereunder are on a principal-to-principal arms length basis and no joint venture or partnership between the Parties has been, or is attempted to be constituted under the terms of this agreement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.20\",\n      \"description\": \"Enforcement\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"In the event either Party shall resort to legal action to enforce the terms and provisions of this agreement, the prevailing Party may recover from the other party the costs of such action including, without limitation, reasonable attorneys' fees.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.21\",\n      \"description\": \"Severability\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"If any provision or part of this agreement is or should become invalid, illegal or unenforceable in any respect, then such invalidity, illegality or unenforceability shall not affect nor impair the validity, legality or enforceability of any other provision in this agreement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.22\",\n      \"description\": \"Entire Agreement\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"This agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the Parties with respect to the subject matter hereof and supersedes prior negotiations, representations, or agreements, either written or oral.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"CL.23\",\n      \"description\": \"Survival of Obligations\",\n      \"clauseText\": \"Any provision or covenant of this agreement, which expressly, or by its nature, imposes obligations beyond the expiration, or termination of this agreement, shall survive such expiration or termination.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"